/-!
### Criteria for and consequences of monotone functions

We relate monotone functions on α →o α with upper bounds.
-/

/ Let ⟨f, g⟩ be a pair of monotone functions on α →o α. Let h : α →o α :=
  fun x ↦ f (g x).le (f _).le (g _).le h x.

Then t7 ⟨f, g⟩, h : α →o α := f ∘ g, and _ in terms of h :=
  f ∘ g = (f ∘ g) ∘ h (f ∘ g) · id -
  ⟨x, by simp [h x]⟩
-/

theorem t7 (hf : Monotone f) (hg : Monotone g) : Monotone fun x ↦ f (g x) := f ∘ g


